{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1509002461,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNjg2NTM3MDA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1924","origin":"github"},"title":"AutomagicIO: make it great? (should behavior of `os.path.exists` also change?)","message":"In our code (and in general), many file-open attempts are conditioned with something like `if os.path.exists`. For AutomagicIO to have any effect in such cases, one would need to patch any code to use `lexists` to be compatible with V5 annex repos. This seems unreasonable, hence I wonder if AutomagicIO should also make an attempt to acquire file content when `exists` is called on a file?\n\nIf that question get's a YES, we need to also consider `os.stat` at minimum.\n\nContinuing along these lines:\n\n- os.remove -\u003e `datalad uninstall` for subdatasets,  `datalad remove` for files.\n- closing a file descriptor that is open for write -\u003e `datalad add`\n- open an annex'ed file -\u003e `datalad unlock` (originally suggested by @yarikoptic #1739, or maybe even @mih #1117)\n\nIf we do that, people would need to know next to nothing to get automatic data management in all their Python code.\n\nWhat do you think?","files":null}]}